


NMCOLL(1)	    UNIX Programmer's Manual		NMCOLL(1)



NAME
     nmcoll - find name collisions in object files (2BSD)

SYNOPSIS
     nmcoll file ...

DESCRIPTION
     _N_m_c_o_l_l scans a set of object files as produced by the assem-
     bler (typically ending with ._o) and produces a listing of
     suspicious name duplications.  _N_m_c_o_l_l is useful when porting
     programs that were developed with compilers that support
     flex (long) names to 2.10BSD which only supports seven sig-
     nificant characters in external names.

SEE ALSO
     a.out(5)







































